# Unity-generated, all reproducible from Assets/ + ProjectSettings/ + Packages/.
Library/
Temp/
Obj/
Build/
Builds/
Logs/
UserSettings/
MemoryCaptures/
Recordings/

# Test + tooling output. The bare *.log catches the batchmode transcripts that
# land at the repo root (test-run.log, scene-build.log, content-build.log and
# the ad-hoc e1/m5/tmp-bootstrap ones) - nine of them had accumulated untracked,
# which is exactly the debris a banned `git add -A` would have swept into a
# commit. Nothing tracked matches, so this hides no history.
test-results*.xml
tools/screenshots/
*.log
reports/

# rig_actor.py's review artifacts -- regenerated every run, meant to be
# looked at locally before trusting a cut, never committed (same posture
# as preview.png already had by convention before this line existed).
# Their .meta siblings too -- Unity auto-imports anything it finds under
# Resources/, including these, and a git-tracked PNG-but-not-its-.meta
# would fail CLAUDE.md gotcha #2's own rule the moment someone committed
# it by habit; simplest to keep both out entirely, same as the PNGs.
Assets/_Project/Resources/Rigs/**/preview.png
Assets/_Project/Resources/Rigs/**/preview.png.meta
Assets/_Project/Resources/Rigs/**/wiggle.png
Assets/_Project/Resources/Rigs/**/wiggle.png.meta

# IDE
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.csproj
*.sln
*.user

# ...except the dotnet host for the Domain tests, whose whole point is that
# it is committed and reproducible. The blanket *.csproj rule above exists
# for the ones Unity regenerates from the asmdefs on every open; these two
# are hand-written and are the source of truth for what the fast test loop
# compiles, so they have to survive it.
!tools/domain-tests/**/*.csproj
tools/domain-tests/**/bin/
tools/domain-tests/**/obj/

# Python bytecode from the tools/ measurement scripts, which import each other
# rather than each carrying its own copy of the constants they parse.
tools/__pycache__/
